// ============================================================
// CODING STANDARDS — AI AND HUMAN CONTRIBUTORS
// ============================================================
// ALL variable names, function names, API endpoint paths,
// JSON field names, constants, and code identifiers MUST be
// in plain English.
//
// The ONLY exception is text directly facing the end-user
// (UI labels, error messages, translated strings) which live
// in the translation layer (TRANSLATIONS object / t() function).
//
// Examples:
//   ✓  item.quantity   item.name   item.description
//   ✗  item.quantity     item.navn   item.beskrivelse
//
//   ✓  function loadInventoryPage()
//   ✗  function loadInventarPage()
//
//   ✓  GET /api/inventory
//   ✗  GET /api/inventar
//
// When in doubt: if a native English speaker wouldn't
// recognise the word as English, rename it.
//
// ============================================================
// FEATURE TRACKING — MANDATORY FOR ALL NEW FEATURES
// ============================================================
// Every new feature or significant change added to this project
// MUST be documented in the wishlist page (pg-roadmap) in
// index.html under the relevant section with status
// «🔬 Under testing» before or immediately after implementing.
//
// This ensures that if the Lab instance (ddos-lab) crashes
// and needs to be redeployed from scratch, no in-progress
// features are lost or forgotten.
//
// Workflow:
//   1. Add feature to the wishlist as "Under testing".
//   2. Test in Lab (ddos-lab).
//   3. Mark «✅ Klar for release» when stable.
//   4. Included in next production update (naf-events, dwod).
// ============================================================

